Expected elements: present

Every must-show item is on the page and in the right place: nav with brand and resolver; the affirmative `Real Aztec mainnet data` banner with its slug and producer sentences, sitting in the content column on the same 504 px left edge as the breadcrumb below it; the hero with full hash and `Succeeded`; the `Not observable` card with the published pruning reason; Overview with block, canonicality, finality and cost; all six content sections in the permanent tense; the provenance strip with all three marks drawn; and the footer disclosure, correctly not claiming this page is demo data. Nothing forbidden is present. Structurally the page is sound: one left edge holds for every block, both tables share a 161 px label column, card padding is a consistent 26 px, and there is no overflow, clipping or horizontal scroll.

What is inconsistent is width and section rhythm. The page declares a 911 px column (rules, both tables and the Raw block all end at x=1415), but every prose card stops at x=1203, and the banner alone keeps the full 911 px box while capping its text near 630 px, leaving ~280 px of empty white down its right side. Section lead-ins come in two sizes: ~131 px plus a rule for Overview, Decoded input, Events and Raw; 55 px and no rule for Internal calls and State changes, whose headings then sit only 32 px above their own cards.

Highest-priority fixes: give the banner the same 700 px prose box the other cards use, and give all six sections one lead-in.

Rating: 7/10

